<blockquote class="uncited"><div>If you are saying the numbers you press in the microphone are not correct then that is normally an indication of a microphone fault. Try cleaning and reseating the connecting cable. The microphone buttons are sent as varying voltages to the main unit. Any poor connection can cause this voltage to be incorrect. <br><br>Colin G4EML</div></blockquote>i second this, it's a known issue with the 9600 radios, especially in a vehicle parked outdoors due to humid air etc. it will happen sooner or later! Also may cause audio problems while transmitting.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3963">VE4HTO</a> — Wed Feb 26, 2025 5:53 pm</p><hr />
